{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1552832590,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MjE5MjgyOTc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3236","origin":"github"},"title":"Improve (automated) commit messages","message":"ATM automated commit messages (\"Added content\", \"Recorded changes\", ...) are useless.\nSome (if not majority) of the commands, e.g. `*create` do not even allow to have commit message specified.  I wonder if we could improve upon that.\n\nIn many cases the intention/result of the command is clear. e.g. if I `create .../subds`, I think it would be better to commit \"Added subdataset subds\" and \"Recorded changes caused by \"Added subdataset subds'\".  If there is multiple objects of action, they could be quantified (`X files, Y datasets`, etc).  And I think it should be possible if we collect a list of actions which were taken by the command before `*save` was invoked.\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eI do something like that in the (good, khe khe) and (definetely) old crawler:\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n```\n    [DATALAD] Added files from extracted archives\n    \n    Files processed: 6202\n     skipped: 4\n     +annex: 6168\n    Branches merged: incoming-\u003eincoming-processed\n\ncommit c6259378478bbcc634b3295b0c710886b9eecb01 (origin/incoming, synced/incoming, incoming)\nAuthor: Yaroslav Halchenko \u003cdebian@onerussian.com\u003e\nDate:   Tue May 16 23:20:05 2017 -0400\n\n    [DATALAD] Updated git/annex from a remote location\n    \n    URLs processed: 34\n    Files processed: 35\n     skipped: 34\n     +git: 1\n```\n\u003c/details\u003e","files":null}]}